{"title":"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Graph)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Graph)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Completing_the_Square)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Completing the Square)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For how many integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/9/4599515bf98090f6552262f1a5d8b6b4e7f6e39c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4-51x^2+50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" /> negative?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/c/01c572433b36181f15913d9761b55cbe6dd0a913.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf {(A) } 8 \\qquad \\textbf {(B) } 10 \\qquad \\textbf {(C) } 12 \\qquad \\textbf {(D) } 14 \\qquad \\textbf {(E) } 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"389\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/f/2cf23ed66ff07116998d77f098512f018a7be72f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50+1=51$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />, so we factor the polynomial as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/2/632c5b4bed28e674fca902468be8b2b23275640b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^2-50)(x^2-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"19\" />. \n</p><p>Since this expression is negative, one term must be negative and the other positive. We note that the first term is a lot smaller than the second, so we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/b/7dbd87121303b2d77e3882e33fe562db7cfd13fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-50&lt;0&lt;x^2-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"164\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>Solving this inequality, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3ad5d0adb374a75583ea8b55f34f8c6d71a82fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&lt;x^2&lt;50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />. There are  exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfy this inequality, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/4/dd491beae61c5edef47e329680386410d3404dbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pm \\{2,3,4,5,6,7\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Thus our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/5/2658a68bf4ca0d7f951e2f9f07f9ed75dc70ef71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~Clarity edits by SwordAxe\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/7/5176de6d3e975a5ccf4d2a02e49d5344a548bf0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4-51x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" /> part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/9/4599515bf98090f6552262f1a5d8b6b4e7f6e39c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4-51x^2+50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" /> has to be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/b/5bb90d025068754ea0b56f2889bbbe4e93119683.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-50$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> (because we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/9/4599515bf98090f6552262f1a5d8b6b4e7f6e39c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4-51x^2+50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" /> to be negative), we have the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/8/54877046fd41e5932bda01d8ca1c69f5668e1278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4-51x^2&lt;-50 \\rightarrow x^2(x^2-51) &lt;-50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"307\" height=\"19\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> has to be positive, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/f/94fdcc6fbd0dcd081db5901714c7fe3574ef6ce2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^2-51)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"19\" /> is negative. Then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5b62f4aa44e4a7727c08c3f34b5fa9601a1be9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2&lt;51$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" />. We know that if we find a positive number that works, it's parallel negative will work. Therefore, we just have to find how many positive numbers work, then multiply that by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. If we try <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/3/4c30bb56b31bbcc7533256382af45b150245b2ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^4-51(1)^4+50 = -50+50 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"257\" height=\"19\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> therefore doesn't work. Test two on your own, and then proceed. Since two works, all numbers above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5b62f4aa44e4a7727c08c3f34b5fa9601a1be9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2&lt;51$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" /> work, that is the set {<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/d/69d38f4a998b6012c488399400ee1be980f6ca93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${2,3,4,5,6,7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />}. That equates to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers. Since each numbers' negative counterparts work, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4db2713a807b265001bf321f67c314b4f1ee5500.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\cdot2=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"120\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Graph.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Graph)\">Solution 3 (Graph)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Graph)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As with Solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, note that the quartic factors to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec5f4439dfaba806c4c022dfbc36b9063735ccb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^2-50)\\cdot(x^2-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"19\" />, which means that it has roots at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/4/87405c399c4177d5118b945284eaf1aa0d3694dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-5\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/3/7532deaac4f1f0cec28befbffd3642c1e41b9fba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. Now, because the original equation is of an even degree and has a positive leading coefficient, both ends of the graph point upwards, meaning that the graph dips below the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/4/87405c399c4177d5118b945284eaf1aa0d3694dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-5\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> as well as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/3/7532deaac4f1f0cec28befbffd3642c1e41b9fba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/3/7532deaac4f1f0cec28befbffd3642c1e41b9fba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> is a bit more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/1/7e150ef2740d1a520884ff6775704b94fd30937f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.4\\cdot 5=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"78\" height=\"13\" />) and therefore means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/5/89587a7840ada93ff20302b33398a7f038105901.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-7,-6,-5,-4,-3,-2,2,3,4,5,6,7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"282\" height=\"16\" /> all give negative values.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/d/91d79a6203f4a349b2b5f5fe632da39f398475b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2}=u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />. Then the expression becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/c/8cc184b2627961402ab0452ef368f9faa730c8e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u^{2}-51u+50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"111\" height=\"18\" /> which can be factored as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/1/1117538a74448e88859fe4fa93b1df8e091ca780.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(u-1\\right)\\left(u-50\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" />. Since the expression is negative, one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259cfddec9c3a145121fc1b3ae3dea919d21209b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(u-1\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b9864477edf6d04d11e87ac7a328c389c7ef781.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(u-50\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> need to be negative. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0a68410dcfa3ee2d0e45ff7005e6912a9763e1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u-1&gt;u-50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f930b120ec8494dd5ce0817e4b2181cf42151c68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u-1&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/42610c54711b7c6af1e686370b1f5bc16189cd6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u-50&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" />, which yields the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/b/acb1041811ad7def0d932a37d54a1b2725320e87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50&gt;u&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" />. Remember, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/6/886dbda1f868de71d3eecf1b1a80d7fee540abce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u=x^{2}$\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, this means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a perfect square between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfy this constraint, namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c8e6bf4d57cd6f2bb0d7d43e00f0f442f53b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />. Solving each of these values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> values (as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> can be negative or positive) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/6/c3653d75b9e29e7bc6e78d990953f1d3b18c924d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Longrightarrow \\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"101\" height=\"30\" />.\n~JH. L\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Completing_the_Square.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Completing_the_Square)\">Solution 5 (Completing the Square)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Completing the Square)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/8/b589a88bbabbca91ee3367a5f4a1df94e6f850a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = x^2$\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />. We want to find when the expression is negative, so let's define the quadratic function:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/5/9d53507240fdfdeaaba939a40070d55213efc1fd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y = a^2 - 51a + 50\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>We can complete the square to rewrite this function in vertex form:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/9/b295e3db01c833cde281ad45847c64eb3722306a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y = \\left(a - \\frac{51}{2}\\right)^2 - \\frac{2601}{4} + 50\\]\" width=\"223\" height=\"46\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87f493f154ef298947e9536badb6ef424479d21d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y = \\left(a - \\frac{51}{2}\\right)^2 - \\frac{2401}{4}\\]\" width=\"181\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>This represents a parabola that opens upwards with its vertex located at:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/2/c922e88a3fa767fc2ad4856c5d78c8e7ba60965d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{51}{2}, -\\frac{2401}{4}\\right)\\]\" width=\"104\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Since the vertex lies below the axis, the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is negative (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/8/d98424e07dba484162112ed0575862bd8fcf880b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />) between its two boundary intercepts. To find where the parabola crosses the axis, we set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a06334068417b1781d14e8b28af827907961eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/8362feedf47d1cd14752e092340457fc84dbff4b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(a - \\frac{51}{2}\\right)^2 - \\frac{2401}{4} = 0\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"46\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/3/5f3e3d0e4b57ec8208e7e1f3f257db6ab53c2111.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(a - \\frac{51}{2}\\right)^2 = \\frac{2401}{4}\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>Taking the square root of both sides gives:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/0074750d342e49e109685a47931dc0f97e3026e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a - \\frac{51}{2} = \\pm \\frac{49}{2}\\]\" width=\"112\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/692f6980bee5615d37c417fc331feab5728ec092.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = \\frac{51}{2} \\pm \\frac{49}{2}\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>This gives our two boundary intercepts for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />:\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/a/91ae3b39a859e072ae478aa2fb26025be5c36e15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{51}{2} + \\frac{49}{2} = \\frac{100}{2} = 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"200\" height=\"38\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caabca84e43f0ffb1d4a752d93d1329fabf97238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{51}{2} - \\frac{49}{2} = \\frac{2}{2} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"173\" height=\"38\" /></li></ul>\n<p>Therefore, the function is negative when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/c/31cc0cd2465722f4b650c004154d76691fb070f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 &lt; a &lt; 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"15\" />. Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/8/b589a88bbabbca91ee3367a5f4a1df94e6f850a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = x^2$\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> back in:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/c/12c87b48b5f3f3760724ef131c32777bb8947290.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 &lt; x^2 &lt; 50\\]\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>The integer values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfy this are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/0/8c0d0dbd3d26182f36b95c2bce6e244263cbe9f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\pm 2, \\pm 3, \\pm 4, \\pm 5, \\pm 6, \\pm 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"216\" height=\"17\" />. Counting these values gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/2/0d2f16950c7b6177e4369d317ee7857b5314c853.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 2 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> possible integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/7/d3749d1ba3ab3a6927437dd98da70b40558232ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User%EF%BC%9AIcosahedron0288#Created_Pages\" title=\"User：Icosahedron0288\">Icosahedron0288</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B\">2014 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Pro